WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.250
In 1898, a Sikh scholar published
a book with a blunt title.

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.870
In English it means: We are not Hindus.

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.290
Yet the free kitchen at every
gurdwara serves anyone who walks in.

4
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.310
And Sikh prayer ends by
asking for the welfare of all.

5
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.880
Many Sikhs believe God can be
found through other faiths.

6
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:24.690
So why do some Sikhs
insist they are not Hindus?

7
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.670
In this mission, you'll sort
three answers to an old question:

8
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.350
is my religion the only true one?

9
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.280
Then you'll see how Khalsa and non-Khalsa
Sikhs draw the line between Sikh and

10
00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.650
non-Sikh in different places.

11
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.390
Your mission: find out why some
Sikhs insist they are not Hindus.
